<!--
  Status-bar notification icon.

  Android uses ONLY the alpha channel of a notification icon from API 21 on,
  so this is a solid white silhouette rather than the colour launcher mark —
  pointing `ic_launcher` at the status bar renders as a featureless white
  blob. It also has to live in `drawable/`: flutter_local_notifications
  resolves icons with getIdentifier(name, "drawable", ...) and nothing else,
  and `ic_launcher` exists only under `mipmap/`, so the lookup returned 0 and
  every foreground notification threw instead of showing.

  A shopping bag: the marketplace mark, legible at 24dp in a status bar.
-->
